WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.960
For one of Marvel Studios' biggest upcoming
movies, Eternals is keeping a pretty low profile.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.770
If you're still in the dark on the MCU's newest
superhero team, here's everything you need

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.680
to know about them, and how their film fits
into Phase 4 — from its far-reaching connections

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.720
to existing characters to its diverse and
exciting cast.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.900
Eternals was officially announced on July
20th, 2019 at San Diego Comic-Con, and Marvel

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.949
wasted no time in confirming a few details
about the movie — namely, that it's scheduled

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:26.960
to premiere on November 6th, 2020.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.520
Although the film was only just confirmed
at Comic-Con, Marvel fans had been hearing

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.640
news about an Eternals film being in the works
since at least the spring of 2018.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.320
By 2019, word began getting out about which
actors were in talks to star in the film,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.960
and before the film was even announced at
Comic-Con, production was already in its early

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.980
stages in London.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.220
Of course, November 2020 may feel like a long
wait, but Marvel fans will be able to tide

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:52.290
themselves over with the release of Black
Widow on May 1st, 2020 and The Falcon and

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.780
the Winter Soldier on Disney Plus in the fall
of that year.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.580
"I'll do my best."

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.060
"That's why it's yours."

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.700
Even long-time Marvel fans might not be too
knowledgeable about exactly who the Eternals

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.740
are, or the exact details of their role in
the Marvel Universe.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.320
After all, they only first appeared in a relatively
limited run of comic books in the mid 1970s

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.000
and '80s.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.140
Their storyline was revived for a miniseries
by Neil Gaiman in 2006, however, which brought

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.340
the characters into the modern Marvel universe.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.880
So who are the Eternals, and what is their
significance to the Marvel universe?

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.270
According to Marvel lore, an alien species
called the Celestials visited Earth millions

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.480
of years ago and began carrying out experiments
on early humans.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.520
One off-shoot of these experiments were the
Eternals, beings that looked like humans yet

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:44.420
possessed abilities like flight, mind reading,
and an almost unbelievable level of strength

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.120
and endurance.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.160
Their superpowers and resilience made them
essentially immortal and indestructible.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.830
But the Celestials' experiments were also
responsible for the creation of the Deviants,

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.500
another group of humanoids who were burdened
with genetic mutations and grotesque appearances.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.460
Humans mistook the Eternals for gods, and
the Eternals often clashed with the Deviants

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.520
to protect humanity.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.139
However, the Eternals weren't unfailingly
perfect, either — as will likely be depicted

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.380
in the film, they can often be misled and
instigate conflicts among themselves.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.740
At this point, the MCU has introduced a countless
number of characters from the original Marvel

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.240
comics.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.740
But have fans been introduced to any of the
Eternals yet?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.800
Well, kind of.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.959
In the comics, Thanos, who destroyed half
of all life in the universe and was finally

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:29.680
defeated by the Avengers in Endgame, was actually
an Eternal.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.739
And yeah, that might seem a little confusing
— especially since the Eternals were supposed

00:02:33.739 --> 00:02:38.419
to be protecting humanity, not wiping it out,
and tend to be able to physically blend in

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.320
among humans, too.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.160
But Thanos was a bit of a wildcard, because
he also possessed a recessive Deviant gene,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.220
explaining his appearance.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.220
His status as an outlier, however, means you
can reasonably expect that most of the characters

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:52.829
in Eternals will be entirely new to the MCU.

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:57.029
In fact, given that the MCU has never shied
away from streamlining their characters' dense

00:02:57.029 --> 00:03:01.260
histories for the screen, it's entirely possible
that Thanos may not even come up.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.120
Then again…

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.760
"I am inevitable."

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.520
Eternals actually shares a connection with
one other film in the MCU.

00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:14.799
In Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 2, Peter
Quill's father, Ego, tells Peter that he is

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:17.870
a Celestial, and is portrayed as possessing
god-like abilities.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.870
Ego is millions of years old, and is also
able to manipulate the matter of the universe

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:22.360
around him.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.540
By the time we meet him in Guardians Volume
2, he has managed to form a whole planet around

00:03:26.549 --> 00:03:28.799
himself, but he can also inhabit a human body.

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:32.249
"I don't know where I came from, exactly.

00:03:32.249 --> 00:03:38.609
First thing I remember is flickering, adrift
in the cosmos, utterly and entirely alone."

00:03:38.609 --> 00:03:42.720
If you've seen Guardians Volume 2, you'll
know what happens next — and if you haven't,

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.640
then let's just say that Ego isn't quite as
benevolent as he first appears.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.760
It's also probably safe to say that Celestials
clearly aren't an all-powerful force for good

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:51.500
in the universe.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.459
There's a good chance they're going to show
up once more during Eternals too, and judging

00:03:55.459 --> 00:03:58.819
by how they've come across so far, there's
a good chance they could be driving the movie's

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.900
primary conflict.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.340
Unfortunately for spoiler-hungry Marvel fans,
pretty much everyone involved with Eternals

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.320
is keeping the movie's exact details largely
under wraps.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:13.080
As of right now, the only real clues anyone
has about the plot come from a few vague comments

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:15.930
from studio president Kevin Feige after Comic-Con.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.370
He told ComicBook.com:

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.620
"It will be a story that will introduce you
to this incredibly eclectic group of immortals,

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.000
they're the focus of the story.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.720
[...] The Celestials go back a long way.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:26.320
We know a little bit about them.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.740
The Collector told us about Celestials, Knowhere
is the severed head of a Celestial.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.440
Ego was involved with them, but we learn much
more about their agenda and what they've been

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:34.940
up to."

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:38.840
If you want to form your own predictions about
what might happen in the film this early on,

00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:40.860
you'll have to turn to the original comics.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:44.990
There's a good chance the plot will be inspired
by the more recent Neil Gaiman miniseries,

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.980
in which the Eternals have assumed normal
human identities and forgotten their origins.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.500
Sources have also told The Hollywood Reporter
that the film will include a love story between

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.000
Ikaris and another Eternal, Sersi — but
at this point, this is all just speculation.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.200
As of right now, what could actually happen
is anyone's guess.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.300
The cast of The Eternals is rounded out with
A-listers and rising stars alike, and while

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:11.230
big names alone can never guarantee a movie's
success, it seems like Marvel have given fans

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.140
a lot to look forward to nonetheless.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:17.680
For example, Richard Madden, who rose to fame
playing the ill-fated Robb Stark in Game of

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.729
Thrones, has signed on to play Ikaris.

00:05:19.729 --> 00:05:24.449
Ikaris is known as the "Prime Eternal" in
the comics, meaning that he is more powerful

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:25.569
than the other Eternals.

00:05:25.569 --> 00:05:29.820
He is fueled by cosmic energy, and can move
at superspeed and communicate telepathically.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.110
His sheer physical strength and agility also
makes him a formidable opponent in combat.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:38.280
In fact, there's little that Ikaris can't
do, and there's a good chance that Eternals

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.009
will be centered around Ikaris as one of the
main protagonists.

00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:45.180
If it seems like Madden's name has been everywhere
lately, you're not imagining things.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.260
He starred in the critically-acclaimed British
TV series Bodyguard, and also played John

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:53.080
Reid in Rocketman, the musical biopic of Elton
John's life.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.140
"Get in the studio and make some music or
don't.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:56.720
I don't care."

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.220
From the looks of it, being killed off in
Game of Thrones was one of the best things

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.280
that could ever have happened to his career.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:06.720
When word got out that Angelina Jolie was
in talks to appear in The Eternals, the prevailing

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:09.940
rumor was that she would be signing on to
play the Eternal Sersi.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:13.870
But at Comic-Con, it was confirmed that Jolie
was actually playing a different Eternal,

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:14.360
Thena.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.320
In the Marvel Universe, the city of Athens,
Greece was reportedly built for Thena, not

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.100
the goddess Athena, as is the case in our
universe.

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:26.060
In Marvel's history, human beings confusing
Thena and Athena bred hostility between the

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:30.319
Eternals and the Olympic gods of Greek mythology,
eventually leading to an all out war.

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:35.689
In Gaiman's Eternals comics, Thena works as
a researcher at Stark Enterprises and starts

00:06:35.689 --> 00:06:39.370
remembering her past as an Eternal through
a series of recurring nightmares.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.449
Jolie is definitely the biggest name attached
to this film right now, and she's ecstatic

00:06:43.449 --> 00:06:44.720
to be part of the MCU.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.020
She told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.020
"I'm going to work ten times harder.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:51.879
I know what we all need to do, we have all
read the script, we all know what the task

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:55.820
ahead is, and we know what you deserve, so
we are all going to be working very, very

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:56.320
hard."

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:02.139
Madden and Jolie joining the MCU is definitely
big news, but the Eternals casting getting

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:06.060
the most positive buzz right now is Lauren
Ridloff's role as Makkari.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:09.900
You may know Ridloff from her previous work
on The Walking Dead, or her former title as

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.320
Miss Deaf America, which she held from 2000
through 2002.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:17.620
Ridloff was born Deaf, and as one of the few
Deaf actors in Hollywood, she has always wanted

00:07:17.639 --> 00:07:20.469
to see more representation for her community
on screen.

00:07:20.469 --> 00:07:24.419
Now, she has made film history as the first
deaf superhero in the MCU.

00:07:24.419 --> 00:07:28.499
Her casting represents a major change from
the original comics — Makkarri was actually

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.080
a male character, and he wasn't written as
deaf.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:35.039
But the reception to this change has been
positive so far, and fans are looking forward

00:07:35.039 --> 00:07:39.229
to seeing Ridloff's portrayal of Makkari,
an Eternal with the power of super speed.

00:07:39.229 --> 00:07:43.069
At Comic-Con, Ridloff was asked about her
feelings on playing Makkari and becoming Marvel's

00:07:43.069 --> 00:07:44.600
first Deaf superhero.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:45.280
She replied:

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.260
"I do have a son.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:50.279
And he asked me after he read Greek mythology,
he was reading through that, and he's like,

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.220
'What does honor mean?'

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:52.160
This.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.480
This is what honor means.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.320
I'm so honored to be here."

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.120
Overall, the rest of the cast of The Eternals
is pretty stacked.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:04.240
Kumail Nanjiani will be playing Kingo, an
Eternal who rarely uses utilizes his actual

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:04.740
superpowers.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:09.640
Instead, he spent years studying with the
Samurai in Japan and now wields a sword with

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.520
the ability to cut through any material.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:16.580
Brian Tyree Henry will be appearing as Phastos,
who basically develops all of the high-tech

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.380
gear and equipment that the Eternals need.

00:08:18.569 --> 00:08:23.480
Salma Hayek has signed on to play Ajak, who
often has to serve as a diplomat between the

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.420
Eternals and the Celestials.

00:08:24.669 --> 00:08:29.780
This is because Ajak was originally the only
Eternal with the ability to directly communicate

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.740
with their creators.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.229
Don Lee is taking on the role of Gilgamesh,
an Eternal who has fought alongside the Avengers

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:38.560
on numerous occasions, but has been largely
overlooked until now.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:43.360
Lia McHugh, the youngest member of the main
cast, is playing Sprite — as the name suggests,

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.840
she's a mischievous trickster whose pranks
have always gotten her into trouble.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.880
New cast members will undoubtedly be announced
as production continues.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.160
Director Chloe Zhao will be at the helm of
Eternals.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.640
Zhao is a newcomer to the world of Marvel.

00:08:55.649 --> 00:08:59.790
In fact, she's relatively new to Hollywood
in general — she directed her first feature

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.149
film, Songs My Brothers Taught Me, in 2015.

00:09:02.149 --> 00:09:06.149
She's best known for her 2017 contemporary
Western film The Rider, which follows a young

00:09:06.149 --> 00:09:10.100
cowboy after an accident nearly kills him
and brings an end to his riding career.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:14.089
The Rider was nominated for both Best Feature
and Best Director at the 33rd Independent

00:09:14.089 --> 00:09:14.800
Spirit Awards.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.000
Zhao's history as an indie filmmaker makes
her an interesting choice for director.

00:09:19.149 --> 00:09:24.220
This film definitely represents a new artistic
direction for Zhao, but considering her numerous

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:26.600
accolades, there's no doubt that the movie
is in good hands.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.540
Cousins Matthew and Ryan Firpo teamed up to
write the script.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:35.120
The two have one film, Ruin, in pre-production
already, but a release date is yet to be announced,

00:09:35.139 --> 00:09:38.190
and this movie will most likely be their feature
writing debut.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:42.670
In short, it's clear Eternals is filled with
fresh talent — both behind and in front

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.280
of the camera.

